note Exercism-style exercise "nucleotide-count": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/nucleotide-count
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note nucleotidecounts writes how many A, C, G and T the DNA strand holds into o[0] .. o[3] and is
note true; it is false when the strand holds any other byte.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/nucleotide-count
om2
fn nucleotidecounts strand view uchar * o edit ulong * to bool
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
